# Application code — Claude Code only

> **EXCEPTION — PLATFORM FACTORY MODE (2026-07-26).** If the operator has put you in platform-factory
> mode, this entire rule is **suspended for factory work**: slice agents you dispatch DO edit
> `apps/**` and `packages/tbd-schema/**`, inside a slice worktree, scoped to the ticket's `owns`
> paths. See [`platform-factory-mode.mdc`](platform-factory-mode.mdc). Outside factory mode this rule
> applies unchanged. **There is no Claude Code to hand off to any more** — in factory mode, do not
> write a handoff artifact and stop; dispatch a slice agent.

**Default: DO NOT EDIT these files in Cursor.**

Application code is shipped by **Claude Code** on `executor: claude-code` slices via `./scripts/ticket run` (work lands on **`main`** — no `ticket/T-0xx` branches).

## Allowed in Cursor (without extra permission)

- Read / search / explain / review
- Point to lines in critique or handoff specs

## Forbidden unless user explicitly says "Cursor implement this code"

- Any patch under `apps/website/api/src/`, `apps/website/frontend/src/`, `apps/mod/`
- "Fixing" audit findings (C1, C2, etc.) yourself
- Completing plan todos that say `claude-code`

## If the user wants a fix

1. Write or update ticket + `.ai/artifacts/tXXX_claude_code_handoff.md`
2. Tell user to paste handoff into Claude Code

## Exception

`executor: cursor-docs` slices that only touch docs under `docs/` or registry — still **no** app source edits.
